    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0268" n="257" xml:id="pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60F8/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chapin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-17T17:00:00-04:00">August 17, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. Your 41, July 9, 11 a.m.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d187-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Is Department correct in assuming that Czechoslovak Government
                        discontinued issuing certificates on June 28, the date of its confidential
                        note on the subject?</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>What steps will be taken by Czechoslovak Government to preclude issuance
                        of certificates in connection with exports to third countries which may
                        reach the United States in the form in which exported or in some altered
                        form?</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
